[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should I set up from the start? (These go into the spec's global constraints, so every task inherits [0m
[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mthem.)[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mLint + format[39m
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier with autofix. Standard for the stack, catches real mistakes in untyped JS, near-zero ongoing cost.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Unit tests
  [38;5;246mA runner (Vitest or node:test), test layout, and a first passing fixture. This is what covers the pure notification [39m
  [38;5;246mrules.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser: add a task, see it notify, dismiss it. Catches wiring bugs unit tests can't. [39m
  [38;5;246mHeavier to set up and run.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — just build it
  [38;5;246mNo tooling. Fastest to a working page; the notification rules go unverified and regressions are found by hand.[39m
